WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
We seek an expression equal to six and generate several candidates.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
The verifier rejects two plus five and retains one plus five.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.550
Search provides alternatives; the verifier provides evidence for this specific criterion.

4
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:28.900
A persistent record retains three facts with provenance.

5
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:35.750
The current query selects only the relevant fact.

6
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:43.417
Useful memory needs selection and freshness, not merely an ever-longer window.

7
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:51.833
The example updates state with new s equals half the previous s plus x.

8
00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:58.683
Inputs 1, 0 and 1 yield states 1, 0.5 and 1.25.

9
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:06.033
State size stays fixed, but the history is compressed and may lose detail.

10
00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:13.383
From position zero, an action proposes moving two units.

11
00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:20.233
The model predicts position two, but the observation measures one point five.

12
00:01:20.233 --> 00:01:29.417
The half-unit error can revise the model or plan; imagining an outcome is not observing it.

13
00:01:29.917 --> 00:01:36.767
The controller receives a position target and a current-state measurement.

14
00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:43.617
The action moves the system, which may respond differently than predicted.

15
00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:50.967
A new measurement updates the error before the next movement is chosen.

16
00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:58.317
A modification increases correct answers from two to seven in ten memory cases.

17
00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:05.167
That result must retain its conditions and exact test set.

18
00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:12.517
Other tasks remain unmeasured; combining mechanisms does not replace checking where they work.

